if x > 20:
    print('A')
elif x > 10:
    print('B')
else:
    print('C')

What is the exact output printed by the following code?

x = 10
if x > 10:
    print(1)
elif x == 10:
    print(2)
else:
    print(3)

questions.solution:
# Get input from the user
num = int(input("Enter a number: "))

# Check and print the sign of the number
if num > 0:
    print("Positive")
elif num < 0:
    print("Negative")
else:
    print("Zero")
